.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt NOSTROMO-DOCS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nostromo-docs
.Nd read local programming manuals, standards, books and examples
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm menu
.Nm
.Cm c | cpp | man | go | go-examples | python | examples | guide
.Ar topic
.Nm
.Cm rust
.Ar book | std | reference | rust-by-example | embedded-book
.Nm
.Cm llvm | freebsd | lua | versions | --check
.Nm
.Cm language
.Ar c | cpp
.Nm
.Cm python-book
.Ar tutorial | reference | library | c-api | extending | howto | using | faq | whatsnew
.Nm
.Cm go-language
.Op Ar spec | memory-model | assembler | godebug
.Nm
.Cm go-help | go-by-example | knowledge
.Ar topic
.Nm
.Cm library
.Op Ar document
.Nm
.Cm electronics
.Op Ar chapter
.Nm
.Cm manual
.Ar file.pdf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.Nm
opens a terminal topic picker.
.Cm menu
opens the graphical picker and launches a separate documentation window.
Manuals, Markdown and plain text use the terminal pager.
Local HTML opens in qutebrowser and PDF documents open in zathura.
Every reference is read from local files; nothing is downloaded.
.Pp
The language references are the C and C++ manual pages and the cppreference
archive, the C23 (N3220) and C++23 (N4950) working drafts, POSIX.1-2024, the
C++ Core Guidelines, the Rust books present in the selected compiler's sysroot,
the Go specification, memory model, assembler guide and GODEBUG history,
.Cm go doc ,
.Cm go help
and Go by Example, the Python library, books and FAQ, the Lua 5.4 manual,
the Arm procedure call standards and System V ABI for AArch64, the CMake
manuals and the Google style guides.
.Pp
.Cm library
opens a document of the offline library, given by its path under
.Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/library .
Without a document it offers each library entry and then its chapters,
titled by their headings and in the reading order of the book's table of
contents.
The SYSTEMS LIBRARY entry holds the System Design Primer and its solutions,
Awesome Scalability, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 explained, what happens when a URL is
opened, a database built from scratch, Kubernetes the Hard Way, The Art of
Command Line and the pure sh bible.
CIRCUITS LIBRARY holds the MIT 6.002 lecture notes, Lessons in Electric
Circuits and the Logisim guide; ROBOTICS LIBRARY holds books on feedback
control, robotic manipulation, autonomous robots and motion planning; and
PCB AND BADGES holds a PCB design tutorial, the Tildagon badge documentation
and two Hackaday badge schematics.
.Cm electronics
opens a chapter of the electronics guide in qutebrowser, named by its file
without
.Pa .html ,
such as
.Ar 02-dc ;
without one it opens the contents.
Its figures are drawn and animated without scripts, and its formula sheet
links every named equation to its explanation.
.Cm knowledge
opens a chapter of the committed extract of The Book of Secret Knowledge:
tools, services, howtos, lists, one-liners or shell-tricks.
.Cm manual
opens a PDF saved in
.Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/manuals .
.Pp
The
.Cm examples
topics are c, cpp, rust, go, python, shell, assembly, vis and zephyr.
Code blocks keep their indentation.
Embedded HTML and Jekyll tags in Markdown are reduced to their text, and code
is shown as written.
MkDocs notes are shown as quoted notes and content tabs as titled sections.
No example is executed by the reader.
.Pp
Go queries disable module and toolchain downloads.
.Cm go-by-example
takes an example's name in lowercase with hyphens, such as
.Ar closures ,
and shows each program followed by its recorded run.
Python library queries read the installed text manual without importing modules.
CMake manuals are manual pages:
.Cm man Ar cmake-commands .
.Cm versions
reports the installed toolchains, the documentation packages, the pinned
standards and the checksum of each library archive.
.Ss Keys
Use j and k to scroll, / to search, n for the next result and q to close
the pager.
Left and right scroll long example lines.
On the desktop, Super+D opens the documentation menu.
In vis, Space od opens it.
In dvtm, Ctrl+B d opens a documentation pane.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/reference
Markdown examples shipped with the dotfiles.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/library
The pinned offline library that the installer downloads and checks.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/secret-knowledge
The selected chapters of The Book of Secret Knowledge and their license.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/electronics
The electronics guide, generated by the dotfiles from
.Pa .install/electronics .
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/manuals
PDF manuals saved by the user.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/nostromo/OFFLINE-DOCS.md
Installed references, commands and update instructions.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/man
Manual pages for the locally built desktop programs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An invalid or unknown topic exits 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
